# bat configuration (Ubuntu package binary: batcat).
#
# Theme: a dedicated 24-bit Tokyo Night ("night" variant) theme whose
# background (#1a1b26) matches the GNOME Terminal profile. Installed from
# folke/tokyonight.nvim into themes/ and compiled with "bat cache --build"
# (the yadm bootstrap rebuilds it on a new machine). Zero-dependency fallback
# if the theme file is ever missing: --theme="base16".
--theme="tokyonight_night"

# Syntax mapping: these custom shell dotfiles have no extension and are not in
# bat's built-in filename map, so bat renders them as plain text (no
# highlighting). Map them to the Bash syntax. The basename glob also covers the
# copies under ~/.dotfiles-private/home/.
--map-syntax=".exports:Bourne Again Shell (bash)"
--map-syntax=".aliases:Bourne Again Shell (bash)"
--map-syntax=".functions:Bourne Again Shell (bash)"
